#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a New Tournament"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new &chessament; tournament, select <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, enter a name, choose "
"the number of rounds, and click <guibutton>Save</guibutton>. You will be "
"asked to choose a location where you want to save the tournament."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Registering Players"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a new player to the tournament click on the <guibutton>Add Player…</"
"guibutton> button in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pairings &amp; Results"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have finished registering all the players of the tournament, you "
"can now make the pairings for the first round. Go to the "
"<guibutton>Pairings</guibutton> view and click on the <guibutton>Pair Round "
"1…</guibutton> button. A dialog will appear where you can customize some "
"options for the first round. It is recommended that you leave the "
"<guibutton>Sort players</guibutton> option enabled. You can choose the color "
"of the pieces of the highest ranked player, or let &chessament; choose a "
"random color for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enter the results, click on a pairing and choose from one of the "
"supported results at the bottom. You can also enter the results using the "
"keyboard. Pressing <keycap>1</keycap> sets the result to White wins, "
"<keycap>0</keycap> to Black wins and <keycap>5</keycap> to draw. After "
"entering a result, the next pairing without a result is automatically "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Viewing Standings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To view the standings of the tournament, go to the <guibutton>Standings</"
"guibutton> view. From there you can choose to view the final standings or "
"the standings from a previous round."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tournaments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the settings window of a tournament, click on the "
"<guibutton>Settings</guibutton> button at the bottom of the &chessament; "
"window. This section describes the available options in details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section you can set some basic information such as the tournament's "
"name, location, and arbiters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section you can configure the number of rounds of the tournament and "
"the tiebreaks used for calculating the standings. More information about the "
"tiebreaks is available in the <link linkend=\"tournament-tiebreaks"
"\">Tiebreaks</link> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Calendar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this section you can set the tournament's schedule."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tiebreaks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&chessament; supports the following tiebreaks as described in the <ulink url="
"\"https://handbook.fide.com/\"><acronym>FIDE</acronym> Handbook</ulink>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Average Buchholz of Opponents (<acronym>AOB</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Buchholz (<acronym>BH</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of Games Played with Black (<acronym>BPG</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of Games Won (over the board) (<acronym>WON</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Number of Games Won with Black (over the board) (<acronym>BWG</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of Wins (<acronym>WIN</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rounds one Elected to Play (<acronym>REP</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sonneborn-Berger (<acronym>SB</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Points (<acronym>PTS</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Progressive (<acronym>PS</acronym>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rating lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To ease the entering of new players in a tournament, you can use rating "
"lists. To add a new rating list to &chessament;, select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Chessament…</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> and go to the <guibutton>Rating Lists</guibutton> "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "&chessament; supports the following rating lists:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"International Chess Federation (<acronym>FIDE</acronym>): combined list, "
"<acronym>TXT</acronym> format."
msgstr ""

